  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- `pass_link` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/ladder_links.rs`): a ladder that opts in (`Motion::with_solid_restart`) and whose user asked for a helix, ramp or arc entry enters a pass start in material (`plunge_law::into_solid`) by the new `entry_restart`. Before, a centre-cutting tool plunged straight down there, with no note.\r\n- `entry_restart` (`descent_dive.rs`): the asked arm where the helix closes on the pass start or links to it at depth. Else a ramp along the pass. Else a plunge. Each stand-in has a note with the site, the level Z and the reason.\r\n- `pocket_hsm.rs`: each piece of the area after the first keeps the `dive_room` start. The note says \"entered at\" (not \"by an axial dive\") when the entry is not Plunge. The pass link gives that start the helix. (The first head added a `choose_entry` seed. The review showed that it changed no result, so commit 1ba90baf2 removed it.)\r\n- `pocket_emit.rs`: Pocket, rest 2D and Adaptive opt in. Contour, slot and trace do not opt in (follow-up #2269).\r\n- Not changed: plunges into a cleared column or into air, operations with a Plunge entry, the rule for tools that are not centre-cutting, all verify checks, the post gate and all refusals.\r\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2265-adaptive-entry-each-region.md`. Cause findings: issue comment on #2265.\r\n\r\n## Readings and pinning tests\r\n\r\nNew `crates/motion/tests/adaptive_entry_pieces.rs` (5 tests). Fixtures: two separate 30x30 pockets; a channel round a standing part plus a separate pocket. D10, two levels, helix entry.\r\n- `each_piece_of_an_adaptive_pocket_gets_the_helix_at_each_level`\r\n- `offset_rings_enter_each_piece_by_the_helix`\r\n- `an_outside_channel_and_a_pocket_name_every_plunge_into_material`\r\n- `a_tiny_second_piece_names_its_plunge_stand_in_at_each_level` (review fix: the named plunge stand-in, with site and level Z)\r\n- `a_narrow_second_piece_names_its_ramp_stand_in_at_each_level` (review fix: the named ramp stand-in)\r\n\r\nThe helix test now requires a descending arc turn on each piece at each level, not only a non-axial descent.\r\n\r\nThe three tests fail on `origin/main` (e808c9629) with \"piece 2 not entered by a helix or ramp at Z -4\" and \"the channel not entered by motion at Z -4\". They pass with the fix.\r\n\r\nGate (local, debug, `-j 6`):\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion`: 94 test binaries, all pass.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- `camcraft-app` suites run one by one with `--test`: golden_cl, solid_law_goldens, adaptive_trochoid, arc_entry, rest_pocket, operations, conformance, regression_models, program_entry, stock_engine_agreement, pocket3d_hsm, posting, recorded_post_streams, carvera_post, tinyg_post, tormach_post, program_units, probe_op, wire_burnout. All pass.\r\n\r\n## Goldens changed\r\n\r\nNone. No golden CL or G-code file changed.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` for `camcraft-app` as one unit: `crates/app/tests/wire_tool.rs` does not compile on main (#2244, fix in PR #2263). The app suites above ran one by one instead.\r\n- The maintainer's `fig8` project was not run through the GUI.\r\n- No real control run was made. No G-code from this change ran on a machine.\r\n\r\nChangelog: 2D Adaptive and Pocket now enter each separate area, and each ring in material, by the helix or ramp entry that you set. A plunge into material that stands in for that entry is named in the operation's notes.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\nFixes #2265\r\n\r\n",
